     "explanation": "High-value, low-volume deals that require custom implementation, multiple stakeholders, and long procurement cycles call for complex sales — a live person guiding the customer through the process. Sales-as-marketing works for small transactions that need no human touch, and 'the product sells itself' is the exact myth this lesson warns against — no deal this large closes without deliberate, high-touch selling.",
