     "explanation": "Targeting 'the entire global market' rather than a small, dominatable segment is a classic monopoly-question failure, and having no concrete plan to reach the first customers is a distribution-question failure. Strong technology, a good team, and good timing don't compensate for a company that can't clearly say who it will sell to first and how — those are two separate, common ways startups quietly fail.",
