     "explanation": "Believing the future will be worse (pessimism) while still believing that decline is knowable and specifically plannable (definite) is the hallmark of definite pessimism — methodical preparation for an expected, predictable decline. Indefinite pessimism would instead produce generalized anxiety without a specific plan, and both optimism quadrants require believing conditions will improve, not worsen.",
